IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-common`
IMPORT `ctp-core`

-- The compulsory third party (CTP) claim in South Australia -- SEAT OF THE CTP INSURER (and the nominal defendant).
--
-- SEAT: an approved CTP insurer (in South Australia, a licensed private insurer) that receives a notice of claim, or the
-- nominal defendant, which Motor Vehicles Act s 126A(4) and (5) bind in the same way. "Is this claim mine to answer? By
-- when should the claimant have notified me? May I decline to deal with it? What must I do for the claimant, and by
-- when? What damages can be awarded against my insured?" Every question is phrased as the insurer asks it, on facts the
-- insurer could state; the court's judgments are inputs, as the @desc says. The rules are in ctp-core.l4; this module
-- builds its records from plain answers and restates no rule. Its names differ from the injured person's seat
-- (voc-seat.l4), so the two can be imported together; the mirror cases in voc-cases-insurer.l4 check that they agree.
--
-- TEXTS: the Open Australian Legal Corpus texts (not official, possibly out of date); see ctp-core.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

§ `The CTP claim -- the insurer's questions`

§§ `The claim and the notice`

GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, how IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury`, `terrorist` IS A BOOLEAN, `insurance` IS A `The vehicle's insurance`, `on a road` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The motor accident`
`the claimant's motor accident` `the day of the accident` how `terrorist` `insurance` `on a road` MEANS
    `The motor accident` WITH
        `the day of the accident`             IS `the day of the accident`
        `how the vehicle caused the injury`   IS how
        `it was a terrorist act`              IS `terrorist`
        `the vehicle's insurance`             IS `insurance`
        `the vehicle was on a road`           IS `on a road`

@export Is this compulsory third party (CTP) claim mine to answer as the vehicle's insurer, or is it for the nominal defendant (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) ss 99(3), 115, 116, 126A(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident the claim is about
      `how the vehicle caused the injury` IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury` @desc How the vehicle caused the claimant's injury: as a direct consequence of its being driven, of its running out of control, of a person travelling on a road colliding with it while it was stationary (or avoiding that), or in some other way
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by a terrorist act
      `the vehicle's insurance` IS A `The vehicle's insurance` @desc The vehicle's insurance: insured under a South Australian CTP policy (yours, if you are its insurer), under another State's or Territory's CTP law, covered by other insurance the Act accepts, uninsured, or never identified after due inquiry and search
      `the vehicle was on a road` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was on a road (matters only for an uninsured vehicle)
GIVETH A `Who answers the claim`
DECIDE `Is this claim mine to answer` IS
    `who answers the CTP claim` (`the claimant's motor accident` `the day of the accident` `how the vehicle caused the injury` `it was a terrorist act` `the vehicle's insurance` `the vehicle was on a road`)

@export By when must the claimant have given me notice of the compulsory third party (CTP) claim (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(2)(a); Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 4(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `how the vehicle caused the injury` IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury` @desc How the vehicle caused the claimant's injury (driven, out of control, a collision on a road with it while stationary or avoiding one, or some other way)
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by a terrorist act
      `the vehicle's insurance` IS A `The vehicle's insurance` @desc The vehicle's insurance: insured under a South Australian CTP policy, under another State's or Territory's CTP law, covered by other insurance the Act accepts, uninsured, or never identified after due inquiry and search
      `the vehicle was on a road` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was on a road (matters only for an uninsured vehicle)
      `the day it became apparent` IS A DATE @desc For a claim against the nominal defendant, the day it became apparent that the vehicle could not readily be identified, or was uninsured (otherwise any day)
GIVETH A `Notice deadline`
DECIDE `By when must the claimant have notified me` IS
    `the time for the notice of claim (s 126A(2)(a), reg 4(1))` (`who answers the CTP claim` (`the claimant's motor accident` `the day of the accident` `how the vehicle caused the injury` `it was a terrorist act` `the vehicle's insurance` `the vehicle was on a road`)) `the day of the accident` `the day it became apparent`

GIVEN `in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN, `with everything required` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the access authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `why late` IS A `Why the notice was late`, `prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Compliance with s 126A`
`the claimant's notice` `in the approved form` `with everything required` `with the access authority` `why late` `prejudiced` MEANS
    `Compliance with s 126A` WITH
        `the notice was in the manner and form the Minister approves (s 126A(2)(b))`             IS `in the approved form`
        `the notice set out or was accompanied by everything s 126A(2)(c) and reg 5 require`      IS `with everything required`
        `the notice was accompanied by the access authority (s 126A(2)(d))`                      IS `with the access authority`
        `why the notice was late`                                                                 IS `why late`
        `the proper assessment of the claim has been substantially prejudiced by the lateness`   IS `prejudiced`

@export May I decline to consider or deal with this compulsory third party (CTP) claim because of the claimant's notice (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(6)(a), (7); Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 4(2))?
GIVEN `the notice was in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant's notice of claim was in the manner and form the Minister approves
      `the notice had everything required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it set out or came with the claim details, the medical certificate, the police report number and the documents reg 5 requires
      `the notice had the access authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it came with the claimant's signed statement authorising access to records
      `why the notice was late` IS A `Why the notice was late` @desc If the notice was late: the claimant's ignorance or mistake, absence from the State, injury, legal disability, another reasonable cause, or none of these; otherwise `it was not late`
      `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was late, whether the proper assessment of the claim has been substantially prejudiced
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I decline to deal with this claim` IF
    `the insurer or nominal defendant may decline to consider or deal with the claim (s 126A(6)(a))` (`the claimant's notice` `the notice was in the approved form` `the notice had everything required` `the notice had the access authority` `why the notice was late` `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment`)

@export Can the claimant start, or continue, court proceedings on this compulsory third party (CTP) claim (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(6)(b); Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 4(3))?
GIVEN `the notice was in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant's notice of claim was in the manner and form the Minister approves
      `the notice had everything required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant has provided the claim details, the medical certificate, the police report number and the documents reg 5 requires
      `the notice had the access authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant has provided the signed statement authorising access to records
      `why the notice was late` IS A `Why the notice was late` @desc If the notice was late, why; otherwise `it was not late`
      `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was late, whether the proper assessment of the claim has been substantially prejudiced
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the claimant start or continue proceedings` IF
    `the claimant may commence or continue proceedings (s 126A(6)(b), reg 4(3))` (`the claimant's notice` `the notice was in the approved form` `the notice had everything required` `the notice had the access authority` `why the notice was late` `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment`)

§§ `What I must do for the claimant`

@export What must I do for claimants as a CTP insurer or the nominal defendant (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(4), (5))?
GIVEN `I am a CTP insurer or the nominal defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an approved CTP insurer, or the nominal defendant, dealing with claims under Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act
GIVETH A LIST OF `Respondent's duty`
DECIDE `What must I do for claimants` IS
    IF `I am a CTP insurer or the nominal defendant`
    THEN `the duties of the insurer and the nominal defendant to claimants (s 126A(4), (5))`
    ELSE EMPTY

@export By what date must I send the claimant a copy of a record I obtained under the claimant's access authority (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(4))?
GIVEN `the day I received the record` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the record or information under the claimant's access authority
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I send the claimant a copy` IS
    `the day I received the record` `plus days` `the days to send the claimant a copy (s 126A(4))`

§§ `What can be awarded against my insured` -- situation: the claim is being assessed

GIVEN `the September quarter figure` IS A NUMBER, `the 2001 figure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts`
`the September CPI figures for the claim` `the September quarter figure` `the 2001 figure` MEANS
    `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts` WITH
        `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS `the September quarter figure`
        `CPI for the September quarter 2001`                            IS `the 2001 figure`

GIVEN `the March quarter figure` IS A NUMBER, `the 2013 figure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CPI figures for s 52(7)`
`the March CPI figures for the claim` `the March quarter figure` `the 2013 figure` MEANS
    `CPI figures for s 52(7)` WITH
        `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` IS `the March quarter figure`
        `CPI for the March quarter 2013`                                       IS `the 2013 figure`

@export What damages for non-economic loss can be awarded against my insured (or the nominal defendant) on this claim (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 3(1), 52(1), (3)-(8); Civil Liability Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 7)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident (the amounts in force then apply)
      `days the claimant's normal life was significantly impaired` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days the claimant's ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired by the injury
      `the claimant's medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The medical expenses reasonably incurred for the injury, in dollars
      `the claimant's injury scale value` IS A NUMBER @desc The injury scale value (ISV), a whole number from 0 to 100, the court assesses under the Civil Liability Regulations 2013
      `the court finds the case exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the ISV is 10 or less, whether the court is satisfied the non-economic loss is exceptional and the threshold harsh and unjust (s 52(5))
      `the ISV the court uses instead` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the ISV the court bases its assessment on (s 52(6)); otherwise any whole number
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the accident year
      `CPI for the September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2001
      `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July on or before the accident (ignored before 1 July 2014)
      `CPI for the March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter 2013 (ignored before 1 July 2014)
GIVETH A `Non-economic loss answer`
DECIDE `What damages for non-economic loss can be awarded against my insured` IS
    `s 52 -- damages for non-economic loss`
        (`Non-economic loss facts` WITH
            `the day of the injury`                                              IS `the day of the accident`
            `days the ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired` IS `days the claimant's normal life was significantly impaired`
            `medical expenses reasonably incurred`                               IS `the claimant's medical expenses`
            `the injury scale value`                                             IS `the claimant's injury scale value`
            `the court is satisfied under s 52(5)`                               IS `the court finds the case exceptional`
            `the injury scale value the court bases a s 52(5) assessment on`     IS `the ISV the court uses instead`)
        (`the prescribed minimum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures for the claim` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI for the September quarter 2001`))
        (`the March CPI figures for the claim` `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` `CPI for the March quarter 2013`)

@export What is the most that can be awarded against my insured for the claimant's loss of earning capacity, given the court's assessment (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 3(1), 54(1), (2), 56A(2), (3), (5))?
GIVEN `the claimant's past loss as assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The claimant's past loss of earning capacity in dollars as the court assesses it (after contributory negligence)
      `the loss in the first week of incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of that past loss for the claimant's first week of incapacity for work
      `the claimant's future loss as assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The claimant's future loss of earning capacity in dollars as the court assesses it
      `the claimant's injury scale value` IS A NUMBER @desc The injury scale value (ISV) the court assesses (0 to 100)
      `the court finds the case exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the ISV is 7 or less, whether the court is satisfied the consequences for future earning capacity are exceptional and the threshold harsh and unjust (s 56A(3))
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the accident year
      `CPI for the September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2001
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be awarded for loss of earning capacity` IS
    `ss 54, 56A -- damages for loss of earning capacity`
        (`Earning capacity facts` WITH
            `past loss of earning capacity as assessed`       IS `the claimant's past loss as assessed`
            `the part of it for the first week of incapacity`  IS `the loss in the first week of incapacity`
            `future loss of earning capacity as assessed`     IS `the claimant's future loss as assessed`
            `the injury scale value for earning capacity`     IS `the claimant's injury scale value`
            `the court is satisfied under s 56A(3)`            IS `the court finds the case exceptional`)
        (`the prescribed maximum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures for the claim` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI for the September quarter 2001`))

@export What is the most that can be awarded against my insured for gratuitous services given to the claimant by family (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 58(1)-(4); Civil Liability Regulations 2013 (SA) regs 18, 19)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `who cares for the claimant` IS A `Who gives the gratuitous services` @desc Who gives the claimant the free services: a parent, the spouse, the domestic partner, a child, or someone else
      `the claimant's injury scale value` IS A NUMBER @desc The injury scale value (ISV) the court assesses (0 to 100)
      `hours of care a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the services are, or will be, given
      `months of care in a row` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive months the services are, or will be, given
      `weeks of care claimed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of services are claimed for
      `the hourly rate claimed` IS A NUMBER @desc The hourly rate in dollars used to value the services
      `State average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The male full-time adult average weekly ordinary time earnings for South Australia published by the ABS, in dollars (reg 18)
      `the court finds paid care would be needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied the services are reasonably required and that otherwise someone would have to be paid to provide them (s 58(3))
      `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July on or before the accident (ignored before 1 July 2014)
      `CPI for the March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter 2013 (ignored before 1 July 2014)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be awarded for gratuitous services` IS
    `s 58 -- the most damages for gratuitous services`
        (`Gratuitous services facts` WITH
            `who gives the services`                                IS `who cares for the claimant`
            `the injury scale value for gratuitous services`        IS `the claimant's injury scale value`
            `hours of services a week`                              IS `hours of care a week`
            `consecutive months the services are or will be given`  IS `months of care in a row`
            `weeks of services claimed`                             IS `weeks of care claimed`
            `the hourly rate claimed`                               IS `the hourly rate claimed`
            `State average weekly earnings`                         IS `State average weekly earnings`
            `the court is satisfied under s 58(3)`                  IS `the court finds paid care would be needed`)
        (`the reg 19 hourly rate for an injury on` `the day of the accident` (`the March CPI figures for the claim` `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` `CPI for the March quarter 2013`))
